surname>Conti</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>St&#x000fc;hmer</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quantal charge redistributions accompanying the structural transitions of sodium channels</article-title><source>Eur. Biophys. J</source><volume>17</volume><year>1989</year><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2548829</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="DurellandGuy1992"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Durell</surname><given-names>S.R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Guy</surname><given-names>H.R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Atomic scale structure and functional models of voltage-gated potassium channels</article-title><source>Biophys. J</source><volume>62</volume><year>1992</year><fpage>238</fpage><lpage>247</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1600096</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Eaholtzetal1994"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eaholtz</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheuer</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Catterall</surname><given-names>W.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Restoration of inactivation and block of open sodium channels by an inactivation gate peptide</article-title><source>Neuron</source><volume>12</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>1041</fpage><lpage>1048</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8185942</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Filatovetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Filatov</surname><given-names>G.N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nguyen</surname><given-names>T.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kraner</surname><given-names>S.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Barchi</surname><given-names>R.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inactivation and secondary structure in the D4/S4-5 region of the SkM1 sodium channel</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol</source><volume>111</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>703</fpage><lpage>715</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9607932</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Greeff1986"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greeff</surname><given-names>N.G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fractionation of the asymmetry current and its relation to sodium channel gating in squid axon</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Ritchie</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Keynes</surname><given-names>R.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolis</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name></person-group><source>Ion Channels in Neural Membranes</source><year>1986</year><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>69</lpage><publisher-name>R. Alan Liss Inc</publisher-name><publisher-loc>New York, NY</publisher-loc></citation></ref><ref id="GreeffandForster1991"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greeff</surname><given-names>N.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Forster</surname><given-names>I.C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The quantal gating charge of sodium channel inactivation</article-title><source>Eur. Biophys. J</source><volume>20</volume><year>1991</year><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>176</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1660397</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="GreeffandPolder1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greeff</surname><given-names>N.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Polder</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimization of a two-electrode voltage clamp for recording of sodium ionic and gating currents from <italic>Xenopus</italic> oocytes</article-title><source>Biophys. J</source><volume>74</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>A402</fpage>(Abstr.)</citation></ref><ref id="Greeffetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greeff</surname><given-names>N.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>K&#x000fc;hn</surname><given-names>F.J.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kathe</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gating current in rat brain IIA sodium channelschanges in ratio between measured gating and corresponding ionic currents</article-title><source>Biophys. J</source><volume>74</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>A402</fpage>(Abstr.)</citation></ref><ref id="HodgkinandHuxley1952"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hodgkin</surname><given-names>A.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Huxley</surname><given-names>A.F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A quantitative description of membrane current and its application to conduction and excitation in nerve</article-title><source>J. Physiol</source><volume>117</volume><year>1952</year><fpage>500</fpage><lpage>544</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12991237</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Jietal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ji</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>George</surname><given-names>A.L.</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name><name><surname>Horn</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Barchi</surname><given-names>R.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Paramyotonia congenita mutations reveal different roles for segments S3 and S4 of domain D4 in hSkM1 sodium channel gating</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol</source><volume>107</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>194</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8833340</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="KontisandGoldin1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="auth